;Match details

* '''Match 1:''' Young guns momentum. '''Face vs. heel''' — Ono & Yamamoto (Seigigun) vs. Viggo & Nakamura (Cannon Club, Junior Tag Champions). The young lions continued their war of attrition against the Cannon Club junior division. Ono and Yamamoto worked fast and smart, isolating Viggo and keeping Nakamura on the apron. At 9:45, Ono pinned Viggo after a springboard DDT. The message: the future is coming for the Cannon Club's junior titles. '''Crowd:''' BIG POP for Ono & Yamamoto. HEAT for Viggo & Nakamura. "LET'S GO ONO" chants. MEGA POP for the finish.
* '''Match 2:''' TV title defense. '''Heel vs. face''' — Tanaka (c, Cannon Club) vs. Sato (Seigigun). Tanaka — still furious after losing to Ono at Episode 6 — took out his frustration on the young high-flyer Sato. The match was a methodical beating: Tanaka used size, power, and underhanded tactics to control the pace. Sato had a brief comeback with a missile dropkick and a rolling cradle, but Tanaka cut him off with a lariat and finished with the Bulldog Bomb at 11:30. Post-match: Tanaka grabbed the microphone and called out Ono — "You got lucky. At Fangatapu, I end you." '''Crowd:''' HEAT for Tanaka. POP for Sato's comeback. HEAT for the Bulldog Bomb. "ONO" chants after the promo.
* '''Match 3:''' Destruction continues. '''Heel vs. face''' — The Marauder vs. Iwata (Seigigun). Iwata was a step up from Morita — quicker, more technical, a better test of whether The Marauder could be outwrestled. The answer was no. The Marauder absorbed Iwata's early offense, caught him on the floor, and threw him into the guardrail. Back in the ring, the running big boot ended it at 7:20. The Marauder is now 4-0 on Wednesday nights. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for The Marauder. "WHO ARE YOU?" chants. GASPS for the guardrail throw. BIG POP for the big boot. The mystery man is becoming a force.
* '''Match 4:''' CHAOS vs. Cannon Club power. '''Face vs. heel''' — Kawada & Takagi vs. Big Stan & Diallo. A rematch from Episode 6, where Kawada and Takagi won. This time, the Cannon Club power team was desperate. The match was a war of strikes and throws. Big Stan dominated stretches with his size, but Kawada's veteran timing and Takagi's lariat turned the tide. At 12:10, Kawada pinned Diallo with a brainbuster — the same finish as the previous week. The Cannon Club's power team has now lost three consecutive tag matches. '''Crowd:''' POP for CHAOS. HEAT for the Cannon Club. "KAWADA" chants. MEGA POP for the brainbuster.
* '''Match 5:''' Tag title chaos. '''Heel vs. tweener/face''' — The Usos (c) vs. Reyes & Kimura, ended in a no contest. The final confrontation before Island Invasion. The match broke down almost immediately — Reyes and Kimura attacked the Usos before the bell, and the brawl spilled all over the arena. Chairs, guardrails, the announce table. The referee tried to regain control but eventually threw the match out at 14:20. No contest. The Usos retain, but the challengers have made it clear: they will do anything to take the titles. Officials separated all four men. The Island Invasion tag title match is now the most violent match on the card. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for the Usos. MEGA POP for Reyes & Kimura's attack. "COBRA" chants. HEAT for the no contest. The crowd wants to see them fight with no rules.
* '''Match 6:''' Kuroshio ghosts. '''Tweener vs. face''' — KAZUKI vs. Kuroki. The two former Kuroshio brothers — now on opposite sides of the Island Invasion main event — met for the first time since the split. Kuroki tried to reach KAZUKI, to remind him of the bond. KAZUKI responded with violence. The match was stiff and emotional, with Kuroki's strong style against KAZUKI's aerial offense. Kuroki kicked out of the Twin Star Press at 2.5, but a second one at 16:45 ended it. KAZUKI defeated his former brother. Post-match: KAZUKI stood over Kuroki, then pointed to the ramp — the message was for Leoni. '''Crowd:''' MEGA POP for both entrances. "KUROSHIO" chants — now mournful. GASPS at the first Twin Star Press kick-out. MEGA POP for the finish. Silence after.
* '''Match 7:''' Family war tag. '''Face vs. heel''' — Leoni & Taumafa vs. Kengo & Malo. The Vaiahi family hierarchy in one ring. The match was a brawl — no chain wrestling, no feeling-out process. Kengo and Malo targeted Leoni's ribs, trying to soften him for KAZUKI. Taumafa and Malo traded heavy shots. Leoni eventually tagged in Taumafa, who ran wild with Samoan drops and lariats. At 18:10, Leoni hit the Spear of Fangatapu on Kengo, and Taumafa pinned Malo with the Samoan Spike. The Chief and the Giant stood tall. Post-match: Kengo rolled out of the ring, staring at Leoni. The family war is coming to Fangatapu. '''Crowd:''' NUCLEAR POP for Leoni & Taumafa. NUCLEAR HEAT for Kengo & Malo. "TRIBAL CHIEF" chants. MEGA POP for the Spear. MEGA POP for the finish.
* '''Match 8:''' Main event. '''Face vs. heel''' — Vance (c) vs. Jusuf Muntasir for the [[IGO Intercontinental Championship]]. The match Vance had demanded. Jusuf brought his Baliscan oil-wrestling style — close-body grappling, leverage through Vance's trunks, heavy throws, and a methodical pace that frustrated the champion. Vance tried to use his technical precision and striking, but Jusuf's unfamiliar style neutralized much of it. The crowd — which had booed Vance for months — began to cheer him. They saw him fighting alone, with no Cannon Club at ringside. Vance made a comeback with a series of forearms and a superplex, but Jusuf cut him off with a thumb to the eye and a low blow in front of the referee. The referee called for the bell at 21:15 — Vance retains by disqualification. Jusuf attacked Vance after the bell, locking in the Abrazo de Terra. Vance fought to the ropes. The crowd chanted for Vance. Vance grabbed a microphone, his voice sharp: ''"You come here from Balisca. You call this a lie. You attack me from behind. You disrespect the belt. You disrespect the crowd. You disrespect every man in this ring."'' — HUGE POP. ''"If your ass thinks pro-wrestling is a lie, then let me show you how real a slap can be."'' Vance slapped Jusuf across the face. Jusuf lunged at him, and the two brawled. Security and officials rushed the ring. The crowd was on its feet. Vance — the former cold heel — had become the man the fans were cheering for. The scripted altercation ended the show. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for Jusuf's entrance. MIXED-to-POSITIVE reaction for Vance — the organic babyface turn is accelerating. "VANCE" chants during the comeback. HEAT for the low blow. NUCLEAR POP for the slap. The show ended with Vance and Jusuf being pulled apart.

== Post-match segment: Vance stands alone ==

After the ring was cleared, Marcus Vance stood alone in the centre of the Aizawa Dome. The Cannon Club had not come to his aid during the Jusuf attack. Kengo, Malo, and the Usos were absent. Vance held the Intercontinental Championship and looked at the crowd — not with his usual cold detachment, but with something closer to recognition.

:''"I came to NOPW to be the best. Not the most popular. The best. And for a long time, I thought that meant standing alone. Being cold. Being above all of you."'' — Mixed reaction, leaning positive.

:''"But tonight — tonight I stood in this ring with a man who thinks everything we do is a lie. And none of the people who were supposed to be beside me showed up. Except you."'' — HUGE POP.

:''"So at Fangatapu, I don't just defend this title. I defend this sport. Against a man who doesn't deserve to breathe the same air as the people in this building. Jusuf — I'm not cold anymore. I'm focused. And you're the problem."'' — MEGA POP.

Vance dropped the mic and raised the Intercontinental Championship. The crowd cheered. The organic babyface turn was complete.

== Backstage: Leoni watches Vance ==

In a backstage segment, Leoni Masua stood in front of a monitor, watching Vance's promo. His arms were crossed.

:''"I told you. A cold man can get lonely. And a lonely man can become dangerous — to his friends, or to his enemies. Marcus Vance just chose. The Cannon Club didn't see it coming."''

The segment ended with Leoni walking toward the entrance ramp. The implication: the Tribal Chief knows that Vance is no longer Kengo's soldier.

