== Aftermath ==

* Marcus Vance completed his organic babyface turn at Episode 7. After retaining the IGO Intercontinental Championship against Jusuf Muntasir by disqualification, Vance cut a promo defending professional wrestling and the fans, then slapped Jusuf and brawled with him. The Cannon Club did not appear during the attack or the promo. Vance left the Aizawa Dome alone, as a champion, and as a face. The Island Invasion match between Vance and Jusuf is now the most personal non-main-event match on the card.
* Jusuf Muntasir lost his first professional wrestling match by disqualification, protecting him while establishing his contempt for the sport. His low blow, post-match Abrazo de Terra, and the slap from Vance set up a heated rematch at Fangatapu. Jusuf enters Island Invasion as a dangerous unknown — a traditional grappler who believes he is exposing a lie.
* The Cannon Club's silence during the Jusuf attack was a major storyline development. Kengo, Malo, the Usos, and the rest of the faction left Vance to fight alone. The fracture between Vance and the Cannon Club is now public and will likely explode at or after Island Invasion.
* Leoni Masua and Taumafa Vaiahi defeated Kengo and Malo in the family war tag match. The win gives the champion side momentum, but Kengo's post-match stare-down showed he remains confident. The Vaiahi family war will be settled at Island Invasion in separate matches.
* KAZUKI defeated Daigo Kuroki, his second consecutive victory over a former Kuroshio member. He has now beaten Ryohei Maeda and Daigo Kuroki, leaving Leoni with no former brothers to stand beside him. The IGO Heavyweight Championship match at Fangatapu is now a pure one-on-one contest between champion and challenger.
* The tag team title match between the Usos and Reyes & Kimura ended in a no contest after a wild pre-bell brawl. The challengers have made it clear they will use any means necessary to win. The Island Invasion match is now expected to be a violent, possibly no-disqualification contest.
* The young guns continued their rise. Ono and Yamamoto defeated two Junior Tag Champions. Akira Sato pushed World TV Champion Jin Tanaka to the limit in a competitive title match. The Cannon Club's junior and mid-card depth is under serious pressure.
* The Marauder defeated Shota Iwata to move to 4-0 on Wednesday nights. The mysterious powerhouse is becoming a significant problem that NOPW will have to address after Island Invasion.
* The Aizawa Dome sellout (10,500) in 11 hours was the fastest in Wednesday night history, breaking the Ogasawara record. The product has now sold out seven consecutive shows in seven markets. The next stop is Fangatapu, Vaiahi Islands, for the biggest event of the NOPW calendar.

